:"b3c4f067-ba17-4f53-b373-50a4c94412c4","timestamp":"2026-08-19T12:26:35.930Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"bin=target/debug/deps/differential-f0ba9144645300f2\nboth_libraries_export_dequantize_granule\nlayout_matches_c\nphase_b_row01_empty_total_bands\nphase_b_row02_all_skip\nphase_b_row03_single_narrow_band\nphase_b_row04_single_wide_band\nphase_b_row05_many_low_bands\nphase_b_row06_unaligned_start\nphase_b_row07_high_bands_only\nphase_b_row08_s_sweep\nphase_b_row09_mixed_bands\nphase_b_row10_full_opcode_range\nphase_b_row11_mod_boundaries\nphase_b_row12_exact_fit_reservoir\nphase_b_row13_one_bit_short\nphase_b_row14_mid_stream_exhaustion\nphase_b_row15_limit_zero\nphase_b_row16_negative_limit\nphase_b_row17_buffer_shapes\nphase_b_row18_group_size_sweep\nphase_b_row19_negative_group_size\nphase_b_row20_bitalloc_oob_index\nphase_b_row21_pos_overflow\nphase_b_row22_negative_pos\nphase_b_row23_huge_group_size\nphase_b_row24_full_choff_walk\nphase_b_row25_grand_fuzz\nphase_c_e01_reject_returns_zero_but_advances_pos\nphase_c_e02_exact_limit_not_rejected\nphase_c_e03_one_bit_short_rejects\nphase_c_e04_negative_limit_rejects_everything\nphase_c_e05_intmax_limit_never_rejects\nphase_c_e06_negative_pos_reads_below_buf\nphase_c_e07_pos_overflow_passes_limit_check\nphase_c_e08_single_byte_path\nphase_c_e09_large_n_shift_masking\nphase_c_e10_zero_bitalloc_skips_band\nphase_c_e11_zero_total_bands\nphase_c_e12_non_positive_group_size\nphase_c_e13_bitalloc_index_out_of_bounds\nphase_c_e14_mod_shift_count_over_31\nphase_c_e15_mod_equals_one\nphase_c_e16_ba_16_boundary\nphase_c_e17_ba_17_boundary\nphase_c_e18_ba_1_boundary\nphase_c_e19_ba_255\nphase_c_e20_choff_drift_writes_past_grbuf\nphase_c_e21_return_value_overflow\nphase_c_e22_null_grbuf_without_writes\nphase_c_e23_null_buf_with_rejecting_limit\nphase_c_e24_full_bitalloc_domain_sweep\ntotal: 51","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_36ikyzfhca4yzekymi6uhswgz6uzpuki6h7d542lwn63spcrdocq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification is complete. All four phases pass.\n\n## What I found and fixed\n\n**One real translation bug** (Phase A/B): the Rust used `(*sci).bitalloc[i as usize]`, a bounds-checked slice index. C's loop bound is `2 * total_bands` (up to **510**) while `bitalloc` is only 64 bytes, so C reads unchecked through `scfcod` and past the struct. Any `total_bands > 32` made Rust **panic/abort** where C returns data. Fixed with a raw pointer derived from the struct base via `offset_of!`.\n\n## Completion gate\n\n- [x] **`SYMBOLS.md`** — C `.so` exports exactly one symbol, `dequantize_granule`; Rust `.so` exports it too. `nm -D` diff is **empty** in both directions, for both debug and release. Zero non-libc undefined symbols. `get_bits` is `static` in C and correctly stays private. Nothing was stubbed — the whole 43-line TU is translated.\n- [x] **Phase B** — all **25** `CONFIGS.md` rows pass, ~15,000 randomized cases (seeded xorshift64*), driving both the wrapper and the low-level `get_bits` paths.\n- [x] **Phase C** — all **24** `ERRORS.md` rows have a passing differential test asserting the *same* sentinel/behavior, not just \"both failed\".\n- [x] **Every feature combination** — `Cargo.toml` has no `[features]` and the C has no `#ifdef`, so there is exactly **1** valid combination; `run_verification.sh` enumerates the powerset mechanically and confirms it.\n\n## Notable C quirks replicated and pinned by tests\n\n`bs->pos` advances even on rejection; `pos + n == limit` is *accepted* (`>` not `>=`); `pos += n` signed overflow makes the check spuriously pass; `choff` initialized outside the `j` loop; `ba == 48` ⇒ `2 << 31 == 0` ⇒ `mod == 1`; all shift counts ≥ 32 masked to `& 31`; `group_size * 4` wrapping.\n\n## Evidence the suite has teeth\n\nI injected **20 mutants** into `src/lib.rs`: **14 killed**. All 6 survivors were *proven* equivalent or unobservable (e.g. `pos & 7` ≡ `pos.rem_euclid(8)`; `choff` reset inside the `j` loop is equivalent because `2*total_bands` is always even). The translation also matches the C built at **-O0, -O1, -O2 and -O3**.\n\nTwo things worth flagging: the harness models `get_bits`'s access pattern exactly and **skips + counts** the residual cases where C itself dereferences a wild address hundreds of MB away (a genuine C segfault, not a divergence) — each such mechanism is separately covered by an observable case, and every test asserts a minimum number of cases actually ran. Also, `cargo test` alone does not emit the cdylib, so the tests include a staleness guard; use `./run_verification.sh`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1180,"cache_read_input_tokens":217716,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1180,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bde487b0-43b2-4a9c-9ba4-46960388e887","uuid":"9fec2ef0-441e-4035-a231-35efde566cc7","timestamp":"2026-08-19T12:26:51.369Z"}
